course: dictionary
lesson: 9610
title: Stripy: having stripes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Stripy is a describing word. It tells you what something looks like. «A stripy head peeps out of a hedge» tells you the head has stripes, so stripy means having stripes.
explain: The words around it give you clues. A head and a hedge do not tell you about stripes, so the word must describe the head. Try the swap: «a striped head» still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Stripy shows up in lots of places, such as stripy jumpers, stripy socks and stripy deckchairs. It can also describe animals. «The okapi's stripy legs break up its outline in the shadows» tells you the stripes help it hide.
fact: Stripy means having stripes: long thin lines or bands of different colours.
fact: Stripy is an adjective, so it describes a noun. It can change to stripier and stripiest.
fact: «Stripy» is used for jumpers, socks, tigers, deckchairs and piglets.
fact: Zebras and tigers have stripy fur or skin, and the stripes can help them blend in with their surroundings. This is called camouflage.
fact: The okapi lives only in the Congo forest and is the giraffe's closest living relative. Its stripy legs help it hide in the shadows.
exercise: What does stripy mean? | Having dots all over | *Having long thin lines or bands of colour | Very soft and fluffy | Wet and grey
exercise: «The okapi's stripy legs break up its outline in the shadows.» Why are its legs stripy? | *To help it blend in and hide | To make it look taller | To make it run faster | To keep it warm in the cold
exercise: «She wore a red and white stripy jumper.» Find and copy the word that describes the jumper. | she | jumper | wore | *stripy
test: Who is the stripy head in the sentence «A stripy head peeps out of a hedge»? | *Badger | Wild boar | Okapi | Giraffe
test: Which sock is the stripiest? | A sock with one thin line | *A sock with many bright, thick stripes | A sock with a small dot | A plain blue sock
exam: Ben says the okapi's «stripy legs» are just for decoration. What do the words around the word suggest? | They help it run faster than other animals | *They break up its outline in the shadows, so it can hide | They show it is a giraffe | They are only for keeping it warm
